			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#256">Nobles Invade Castle Mistmoor</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Friday night, eight daring members of our Noble Alliance conducted an impromptu mini-raid of Castle Mistmoor. The effort was led by Agrivar with the help of Ferriciean. Kaidog, Latrobe, Wizzorton, and Esdepapachasa valiantly slashed their way into the ballroom with buffing and healing support from Faythea and myself. Spio made it to the entrance of the castle zone, but an untimely link death forced him to miss the action within. It should also be noted that we had the help of Rashagan, an Iksar shadow knight who had enlisted my services for a port to Gd, but after hearing of our plans to overtake Mistmoor, elected to join us in the effort. <br />
There were few casualties, but those who fell to the undead foes were quickly resuscitated by Faythea.  Our invasion was brief, but all in all it was successful and rewarding - a nightshade wreath! (Which this druid needed badly and is very grateful for.)<br />
This mini- raid was just a preview of the upcomming great guild raids to come.  As you read this, our Noble Invasion committee is probably planning our next raids. <br />
Will our mid-levels invade Split Paw? or perhaps a seige of Dalnir? Maybe a return to Mistmoor?  <br />
When our Noble Alliance unites on a raid, one thing is certain: The event will be fun for all and we will prevail!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							<br>
														<strong>By:</strong>
							<span class="name"> <a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1891">Kandu Windwolf</a> at 5:30 PM PST - November 10th, 2001</span>
						</td>
					</tr>
